  "body": "Currently clients resolve urls that look like URLs, but there are times when you want to resolve things like MSC numbers or other string patterns which may have a meaning in a subset of rooms. For example, if someone says MSC1234 in the `#matrix-spec` room then I'd like my client to linkify the text to be `[MSC1234](https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-doc/issues/1234)`.\r\n\r\nThis could probably be expressed in a state event(s) and would be opt-in for clients, but would reduce the amount of noise created by bots trying to be helpful by spitting links underneath messages.",
